# Jak 1: the fisherman's game from Jak's eyes, the net in the hand (LIST-0.1.9 item 20; the owner: "making the fishing
# minigame work in first person vr ... motion controls, proper implementation"). Run with JAKVR_TEST_CONTINUE=jungle-start
# JAKVR_TEST_WARP=fisher JAKVR_TEST_RIDE=1 QUEST_SIM_ALIGN=10000 JAKVR_STATE_TRACE=1 (as jak1_fishing.sim) and Fishing
# game in first person on (it starts on): the game starts 3 seconds after the warp, the view in his eyes turned to the
# river ("[vr-view] the fishing game from Jak's eyes"), the net in the right hand ("[vr-pad] ... from Jak's eyes",
# "[vr-body] the fishing net carried"). The hand then points down at the water ahead, to the left, to the right, far
# left with the hand out; the head leans (the net stays); the left grip takes the net in the left hand, the right grip
# back. "[vr] fishing: the net across the river at ..." once a second says where the basket is. Each step about a
# second and a half, all inside the game's first 15 s (missed fish lose it some 17 s in, sim s14 fe); the grips and the
# hands' sweeps make no fists or kicks while fishing.
